00:39:30.455 --> 00:39:31.830
But we also talked
about the fact

00:39:31.830 --> 00:39:33.220
that that's not going to work.

00:39:33.220 --> 00:39:35.940
We need to be able to reason
about namespaces, sources,

00:39:35.940 --> 00:39:38.910
and apply security policy
with that kind of cadence.

00:39:38.910 --> 00:39:42.540
So what we have done is we are
allowing our security operators

00:39:42.540 --> 00:39:46.590
to define, as I mentioned, we're
going to define source groups,

00:39:46.590 --> 00:39:49.020
where we will add all the
services that are going

00:39:49.020 --> 00:39:50.207
to initiate the connections.

00:39:50.207 --> 00:39:52.290
And we're going to add
destination address groups,

00:39:52.290 --> 00:39:53.820
and we're going to
define the services that

00:39:53.820 --> 00:39:55.770
are the recipients
for those connections.

00:39:55.770 --> 00:39:59.760
And then we're also going to add
certain other attributes, which

00:39:59.760 --> 00:40:01.845
will allow us to now
enforce this policy.

00:40:01.845 --> 00:40:04.470
So I'm going to show you how we
are creating the source address

00:40:04.470 --> 00:40:09.760
group, which is essentially
constituted with all

00:40:09.760 --> 00:40:15.450
