is going to be leveraged.

00:41:35.488 --> 00:41:37.020
For example, is it
going to be HTTP?

00:41:37.020 --> 00:41:39.890
Is it going to be
HTTP2, GRPC, et cetera?

00:41:39.890 --> 00:41:44.320
So you can define all aspects
of your service communications

00:41:44.320 --> 00:41:46.180
and represented as
a security policy.

00:41:49.793 --> 00:41:51.460
And I'm actually going
to show you that.

00:41:51.460 --> 00:41:54.690
So you can see that we are
actually referencing the source

00:41:54.690 --> 00:41:58.030
namespace, which is constituted
with all your source services.

00:41:58.030 --> 00:42:00.930
Similarly for the
destination source,

00:42:00.930 --> 00:42:03.540
we have also defined
what is the protocol.

00:42:03.540 --> 00:42:06.270
The service, it's service HTTP.

00:42:06.270 --> 00:42:09.370
And the action is to allow
this kind of traffic.

00:42:09.370 --> 00:42:12.260
So once we have done
this, we can actually

00:42:12.260 --> 00:42:15.270
commit this to Panorama, and
